G2749.def:
κεῖμαι 
[in LXX: Jérémie 24:1 (יָעַד hoph,), al. ;] 
used as passive of τίθημι (LS, see word), to be laid, to lie; 
__(a) of persons: an infant, Luc 2:12, 16; a dead body, Matthieu 28:6, Luc 23:53, Jean 20:12; 
__(b) of things, to lie, be laid or set, stand: Matthieu 5:14, Jean 2:6 19:29 20:5-7 21:9, Apocalypse 4:2 21:16; trop., Θεμέλιος, 1 Corinthiens 3:11; before prep. with accusative, πρός, Matthieu 3:10, Luc 3:9; εἰς, Luc 12:19; ἐπί, trop., κάλυμμα, 2 Corinthiens 3:15. Metaphorical, ὁ κόσμος ἐν τ. πονηριῷ κ., 1 Jean 5:19; to be laid down, appointed: of law, with dative of person(s), 1 Timothée 1:9; before εἰς with accusative (of purpose), Luc 2:34, Philippiens 1:16, 1 Thessaloniciens 3:3 
(cf. ἀνά-, συν-ανά-, ἀντί-, ἀπό-, ἐπί-, κατά-, παρά-, περί-, πρό-κειμαι).†

G2799.def:
κλαίω 
[in LXX chiefly for בָּכָה ;] 
of any loud expression of pain or sorrow, esp. for the dead, to weep, lament; 
__(a) intrans.: Marc 5:38-39 14:72 (M, Pr., 131) Marc 16:10, Luc 7:13, 32 7:38 8:52, Jean 11:31, 33 16:20 20:11, 13 20:15 Actes 9:39 21:13, 1 Corinthiens 7:30, Philippiens 3:18, Jacques 4:9 5:1, Apocalypse 5:5 18:15, 19; πολύ, Apocalypse 5:4; πολλά, Actes 8:24 (WH, mg.); πικρῶς, Matthieu 26:75, Luc 22:62; opposite to γελάω, Luc 6:21, 25; χαίρω, Romains 12:15; before ἐπί, with accusative, Luc 19:41 23:28, Apocalypse 18:9; 
__(b) trans., with accusative of person(s), to weep or lament for, bewail: Matthieu 2:18.†
SYN.: see: δακρύω
